<article class="env-lemma" id="0F5A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0F5A">Lemma <span data-tag="0F5A">63.6.2</span>.</a> Let $j : U \to X$ be an étale morphism. Then $j^! = j^{-1}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $j_!$ as defined in Section <a href="/tag/0F6E" data-tag="0F6E">63.4</a> agrees with $j_!$ as defined in Étale Cohomology, Section <a href="/tag/03S2" data-tag="03S2">59.70</a>, see Lemma <a href="/tag/0F6Q" data-tag="0F6Q">63.4.3</a>. Finally, in Étale Cohomology, Section <a href="/tag/03S2" data-tag="03S2">59.70</a> the functor $j_!$ is defined as the left adjoint of $j^{-1}$ and hence we conclude by uniqueness of adjoint functors. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>